{"author":{"id":"8d2e0405f08ac6c481f912544d6d5c0f58b2dc14a7e51ad4d499ee7a34567943"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1795426304,"nonce":"NSNKepHn6L8DET1kK6HPV3eQ6Jg=","title":"jno.fvm: a Laplacian inside jnn.stack in a vector equation is evaluated per cell, not as a face flux, and silently","message":"Found on feat/fvm (the conjugate gas example). In a vector fvm equation, a term jnn.stack([0, 0, 0, K*(T.xx + T.yy)]) is not a divergence for _split_equation, so it goes to the volume terms and is evaluated cell by cell: not conservative (the gas lost 1.2-1.8x the heat its interface flux said), and no warning fires (_has_noncons_derivative does not see the Hessian inside the stack). Written as stack([0, 0, 0, -K*T.x]).d(x, scheme=\"finite_difference\") + ...d(y) it is a face flux and exact. Fix: split a stacked volume term per component, or at least warn.","files":null}]}